ruxen is a port of nginx and contains material from it:

- examples/mime.types, which the release tarballs and container images
  ship (as /etc/ruxen/mime.types in the images), is nginx's conf/mime.types
  as it is.
- corpus/stubs/ holds nginx's conf/fastcgi.conf, fastcgi_params, koi-utf,
  koi-win, mime.types, scgi_params, uwsgi_params and win-utf as they are
  (proxy_params is Debian's); they are not shipped.
- Text from nginx's C source: the status lines' reason phrases
  (ngx_http_status_lines[]), the built-in error pages
  (ngx_http_special_response.c), and the log and error messages ruxen
  writes as nginx does.

